a:2:{s:7:"current";a:8:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1676832861;s:8:"modified";i:1676832891;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1676832891;s:2:"ip";s:13:"71.210.14.178";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:25:"recipes:baked_potato_soup";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:3;}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:11:"description";a:1:{s:8:"abstract";s:517:"Baked Potato Soup, By Ali Slagle

If we’re being honest, a baked potato isn’t really about the potato. It’s about the toppings: plush sour cream, butter, cheese, salty bacon, bright scallions. This soup version doesn’t skimp on those extras: The potatoes simmer in milk with garlic and scallions until just tender, then they join sour cream and Cheddar in the pot before the toppings — including potato skins — are added. It’s potatoey, creamy and adaptable. Make it smooth or textured, skip the baco…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:3:"mcf";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1676832861;s:8:"modified";i:1676832891;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1676832891;s:2:"ip";s:13:"71.210.14.178";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:25:"recipes:baked_potato_soup";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:3;}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:3:"mcf";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";}}}